      "content": "hindsight bias is a copout imo. i know exactly what i was doing, i wasnt just guessing. the timing was too precise. i mean, if you look at the way high-frequency algos are basically just deterministic sets of rules, isn't it possible they can actually respond to external energetic or cognitive patterns if those patterns hit certain frequencies? like, if i'm hitting a specific mental tempo, and the algos are tuned to specific millisecond intervals, isn't there a theoretical way those two things could interface? i'm not talking about magic, i'm talking about a technical synchronization between my cognitive state and the execution timing of the bots.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
